  "bio": "Elected to represent House District 89 in 2018, Representative Candy Noble is in her fourth term in the Texas House of Representatives. Representative Noble serves on the House Committee on Human Services, the Ways & Means Committee and she has been appointed the Vice Chair of the Ways & Means Sub-Committee on Property Tax Appraisals. Candy is in her second term as the President of the Board of the Texas Conservative Coalition. In 2019, Representative Noble was named an “Emerging Leader” by GOPAC. She was one of only 30 Republican state legislators from across the nation to earn this distinction that year. A strong proponent of education, Representative Noble has a degree in Education from Hardin-Simmons University in Abilene and serves on their.",
